Source: linux-galaxyxr
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Stanislav Aleksandrov <lightofmysoul@gmail.com>
Build-Depends:
 bc,
 bison,
 clang:native,
 cpio,
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 flex,
 kmod,
 libelf-dev:native,
 libssl-dev:native,
 lld:native,
 llvm:native,
 openssl,
 perl:native,
 python3:native,
 rsync,
 xz-utils,
 zstd,
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Standards-Version: 4.7.4
Homepage: https://github.com/rustedsword/samsung_kernel_galaxy_xr
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/rustedsword/samsung_kernel_galaxy_xr
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/rustedsword/samsung_kernel_galaxy_xr.git -b I610UES3AZJ2_fixed

Package: linux-image-@RELEASE@
Architecture: arm64
Depends: kmod, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: linux-firmware
Description: Linux @RELEASE@ for the Samsung Galaxy XR
 The kernel as a plain arm64 Image, which XrBoot starts through its
 EFI stub, its modules, the Galaxy XR device trees (the base trees and
 the board overlays XrBoot builds the tree from) and the options the
 kernel needs on its command line.

Package: linux-image-galaxyxr
Architecture: arm64
Depends: linux-image-@RELEASE@ (= ${binary:Version}), galaxyxr-initramfs-android-crap, linux-firmware,
 xrboot-kernel-install, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Linux for the Samsung Galaxy XR (the newest kernel)
 Depends on the newest Galaxy XR kernel, on xrboot-kernel-install,
 which puts it on XRBOOT, on galaxyxr-initramfs-android-crap and on
 linux-firmware, and blacklists the modules of Samsung's vendor blocklist.
